## Executive Summary & Vision Statement

**KWIN City** (*Knowledge, Wellbeing, Innovation, and Natural City*)—formerly known as KHIR City—is Karnataka’s flagship 5,800-acre mega-project located along the Doddaballapur–Dabaspet–Nelamangala corridor in Northwest Bengaluru. With a planned investment of ?48,000 Crore, KWIN City is designed to shift Bengaluru’s technological, healthcare, and higher education gravity.

Because of rapid developments—including land acquisition notifications by the [Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Board (KIADB)](https://kiadb.in/), construction along the [Satellite Town Ring Road (STRR / NH-648)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satellite_Town_Ring_Road), and major anchor investments like Toyota Kirloskar Motor’s 300-acre Bizintel Hub—there is significant information asymmetry.

By combining real-time spatial GIS layers, survey-number acquisition risk checkers, satellite time-lapse tracking, and investor matchmaking, **kwin-city.com** can position itself as the definitive intelligence utility and transaction catalyst for the region.

